# Portfolio Development Rules

## General
- This is an existing personal portfolio.
- Preserve the existing visual language and architecture.
- Prefer reusing existing components over creating new components.
- Do not rewrite existing components unless necessary.
- Do not introduce a new framework or styling system.
- Follow the existing project's naming conventions.
- Follow the existing file and folder structure.

## Design
- Match the existing typography system.
- Match existing spacing conventions.
- Reuse existing colors and design tokens.
- Reuse existing responsive breakpoints.
- Reuse existing animation patterns.
- Maintain the existing visual hierarchy.

## Components
Before creating a new component:
1. Search the existing codebase for a reusable component.
2. Determine whether an existing component can be extended.
3. Only create a new component when an existing one cannot reasonably support the requirement.

## New Case Studies
- Follow the implementation pattern of existing case studies.
- Keep the new case study consistent with the rest of the portfolio.
- Do not redesign global navigation, footer, typography, or layout unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve accessibility and responsive behavior.

## Code Quality
- Keep components maintainable.
- Avoid unnecessary duplication.
- Keep content and layout reasonably separated.
- Do not make unrelated changes to existing portfolio pages.
